# Only required if you want to override the default values

## WordPress APIs
## important: never leak those to client-side code, keep them secret
WORDPRESS_URL=http://localhost

## WordPress reads: retries of a refused or dropped read (408, 425, 429, 5xx,
## network errors, timeouts), with a jittered exponential backoff
# WORDPRESS_FETCH_MAX_RETRIES=4
# WORDPRESS_FETCH_RETRY_DELAY=1000
## Milliseconds before an attempt with no answer is abandoned. A read stops
## after 45 s whatever this value, retries included: see docs/caching.md
# WORDPRESS_FETCH_TIMEOUT=15000
## WordPress requests in flight at once, per process (each `next build` worker
## is one). A read waiting for a slot fails after 45 s: see docs/caching.md
# WORDPRESS_FETCH_CONCURRENCY=6

## Next.js config
## hint: learn more about Next.js env vars on https://nextjs.org/docs/basic-features/environment-variables
NEXT_URL=http://localhost:3000

## Enables Next-only features in components shared with the WP theme (e.g. image optimisation)
NEXT_PUBLIC_IS_THIS_NEXT=true

## Secret to authorize revalidation. Generate with `openssl rand -hex 32` and keep it secret
REVALIDATE_SECRET=supersecret

## Required: secret WordPress sends to start a preview. Without it, every preview is refused.
## Must match WordPress's `WORDPRESS_PREVIEW_SECRET`, which defaults to `spck`: keep that
## value for local development only, and generate one with `openssl rand -hex 32` elsewhere
WORDPRESS_PREVIEW_SECRET=spck

## Debug: log every WordPress round-trip of `fetchAPI` (see docs/caching.md)
# DEBUG_PERFS=1
